// This example builds a https://vaadin.com/flow[Vaadin Flow] web application
// running on Spring Boot, using the `mill-contrib-vaadin` plugin:
//
// * The module mixes in `mill.contrib.vaadin.VaadinModule`: `./mill run` starts
//   the application in Vaadin's development mode
// * The `prod` sub-module extends `VaadinProdModule`: it is the production build
//   of the same application. `prod.vaadinBuildFrontend` runs Vaadin's production
//   frontend build, the equivalent of the `prepare-frontend` and `build-frontend`
//   goals of the Maven plugin: `npm install` and a Vite bundle in `META-INF/VAADIN`.
//   `prod.run` runs the application with this bundle, and as `prod` also mixes in
//   `RepackageModule`, `prod.repackagedJar` packages it as an executable jar
//
// Development-only dependencies such as `com.vaadin:vaadin-dev` go into the
// `runMvnDeps` of the Vaadin module: `./mill run` uses them, while `prod` leaves
// them out. Runtime dependencies of the production build go into `prod`'s own
// `runMvnDeps`.

/** See Also: build.mill.yaml */

/** See Also: src/com/example/Application.java */

/** See Also: src/com/example/MainView.java */

// The frontend build uses the Flow version of the application's classpath, here
// managed by `vaadin-bom`. Vaadin's build tooling requires Java 21, hence the
// `mill-jvm-version` above.
//
// Frontend sources such as themes, stylesheets or TypeScript views go into
// `frontend/`, next to `src/` and `resources/`; Vaadin also generates files into
// `frontend/generated/`. A `MavenModule` uses Vaadin's default `src/main/frontend`
// instead, and `vaadinFrontendDir` can point anywhere else.

/** Usage

> ./mill show vaadinFlowVersion
"25.3.0"

> ./mill runBackground

> for i in $(seq 1 300); do curl -sf localhost:${PORT:-8080} -o page.html && ! grep -q devServerIsNotLoaded page.html && break; sleep 1; done # mac/linux

> curl http://localhost:${PORT:-8080} # mac/linux
...window.Vaadin.developmentMode = true;...

> ls frontend/generated # mac/linux
...jar-resources...

> ./mill clean runBackground

> ./mill prod.vaadinBuildFrontend
...

> ls out/prod/vaadinFrontendBuild.dest/servlet-resources/META-INF/VAADIN/config
...flow-build-info.json...

> ./mill prod.runBackground

> curl http://localhost:${PORT:-8080} # mac/linux
...<script type="module" crossorigin src="VAADIN/build/indexhtml-...

> ./mill clean prod.runBackground

> ./mill show prod.repackagedJar
...out/prod/repackagedJar.dest/out.jar...

> java -jar out/prod/repackagedJar.dest/out.jar > prod.log 2>&1 & echo $! > prod.pid # mac/linux

> curl http://localhost:${PORT:-8080} # mac/linux
...<script type="module" crossorigin src="VAADIN/build/indexhtml-...

> kill $(cat prod.pid) # mac/linux

*/

// The executable jar runs the application in Vaadin's production mode:
//
// [source,console]
// ----
// > java -jar out/prod/repackagedJar.dest/out.jar
// ----
